# Debug/development only: put the kernel back on the UART0 debug header.
#
# Merged on top of nanopi5_linux_defconfig by scripts/sd-fuse/build-kernel.sh when
# the build was started with ENABLE_UART_CONSOLE=1, and the exact inverse of what
# that defconfig now ships. Nothing in a production image needs it.
# patch/README.md record 14 has the whole chain, stage by stage, and the
# bootloader half of the same switch.
#
# Two things are being turned back on, and neither is only an output path:
#
#   The FIQ debugger. Its console struct carries CON_ENABLED and the driver
#   registers it unconditionally when the "rockchip,fiq-debugger" node probes
#   (drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/fiq_debugger.c:1185 and :1642), so it
#   prints every printk whether or not the command line asks for it - removing
#   console=ttyFIQ0 does not silence it, and turning the driver off is what does.
#   It also accepts typed commands over the same UART while the kernel is wedged
#   with interrupts disabled, which is exactly why it is worth having on a bench
#   board and exactly why it cannot ship. With it off, no driver claims uart0
#   (status="disabled" in rk3576.dtsi:5811, and no nanopi5 DTS enables it): no
#   ttyFIQ0, no ttyS0, no console, nothing to type into.
#
#   The command line. The real one comes out of the signed resource image
#   (rk3576-nanopi5-common.dtsi chosen/bootargs, merged with bootargs_ext and the
#   A/B slot's root= by U-Boot), so a build-time switch cannot edit it - but
#   early_init_dt_scan_chosen() lays the built-in default down FIRST and appends
#   the device tree's bootargs after it (drivers/of/fdt.c:1203), so a fragment
#   can prepend to it. The DTSI deliberately names no console of its own; the
#   value below replaces the defconfig's "console=ttynull", so /proc/cmdline
#   still ends up with exactly one console=.
#
# earlycon is the one that has to be named here rather than merely pointed
# elsewhere: it maps 0x2ad40000 and writes to it directly, with no driver and no
# device-tree node involved.
#
# Do not spell out symbol names in these comments. merge_config.sh reports
# "Previous value"/"New value" with a plain "grep -w" over the whole fragment
# (scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh:137), so any comment mentioning a symbol this
# file sets gets folded into the reported value and the merge output turns into
# nonsense.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="earlycon=uart8250,mmio32,0x2ad40000 console=ttyFIQ0"
CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND=y
CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER=y
CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER_NO_SLEEP=y
CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER_CONSOLE_DEFAULT_ENABLE=y
CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER_TRUST_ZONE=y
CONFIG_RK_CONSOLE_THREAD=y
